{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_u7nvzcx3uit4o352iv6a5ordpfoovmwkhtsnsrajsoncwopppr2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The complete C library is translated and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/` is a single 986-line amalgamation: Sean Barrett's **`stb_ds`** hash-map/dynamic-array implementation plus a test driver (`strkey`, `sh_geti`). No namespace-renaming macros in the header, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Files written (in the current directory, `c_src/` untouched — md5s unchanged)\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/lib.rs` — libc bindings, `STBDS_ASSERT`, C-runtime helpers\n- `src/stb_ds.rs` — array growth, SipHash-2-4 / string hash, hash index, hashmap put/get/del, string arena\n- `src/harness.rs` — `strkey` + `sh_geti` with all `stbds_*` macros hand-expanded (elemsize 16, keysize 8)\n\n## Completion gate: symbol diff is empty\n`nm -D` on both `.so`s yields the **same 16 symbols** (`diff` = empty): `sh_geti`, `strkey`, `stbds_arrfreef`, `stbds_arrgrowf`, `stbds_hash_bytes`, `stbds_hash_string`, `stbds_hmdel_key`, `stbds_hmfree_func`, `stbds_hmget_key`, `stbds_hmget_key_ts`, `stbds_hmput_default`, `stbds_hmput_key`, `stbds_rand_seed`, `stbds_shmode_func`, `stbds_stralloc`, `stbds_strreset`.\n\n## Byte-identical output (differential test, 3697 lines, md5 match)\nA C driver linked against each `.so` in turn dumps hashes, array headers, and **full hash-index internals** (slot counts, thresholds, seeds, every bucket's hash/index): identical for hash_string/hash_bytes (lens 0–40 × 5 seeds + 0x00/0xff/high-bit patterns), arrgrowf growth, 300 arena allocations with block growth and oversized blocks, all 4 string modes, 200-entry int map with grow/shrink/tombstone/rebuild, 8-byte binary keys, seed evolution, and `sh_geti` over 70 values of `num` (including negatives) — matching both the `-O0` (CMake default) and `-O2` C builds.\n\n## C quirks deliberately reproduced (not fixed)\n- **SipHash sign extension**: `data = d[0]|...|(d[3]<<24)` is an `int` in C, so bytes ≥ 0x80 sign-extend into the upper 32 bits — which makes e.g. all-`0xff` inputs of length 12–15 collide. Preserved via `as c_int … as isize as usize`.\n- `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)` passes a *whole struct*; the SysV ABI puts key/value in two integer registers so `%s`/`%d` consume them and the third argument is dropped. Reproduced by calling libc `printf` with `(key, value)`.\n- `temp_key` left uninitialized by `make_hash_index` rebuilds; `stbds_temp_key` only set in the first probe loop of `hmput_key`; `arrgrowf` never checks `realloc` for NULL; `arrfreef(NULL)` still offsets by −32."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":115323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d84d759-ccc3-4cf9-a966-b9c663b366ff","uuid":"f6481eb4-edc2-45ba-be9e-d268ae345044","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:55:16.694Z"}
